From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: keyboard focus, KeyDown/KeyUp, GotFocus/LostFocus; typing into a TextBox

XAML islands took no keyboard: a TextBox could not be typed into and KeyDown, KeyUp, GotFocus and LostFocus handlers were accepted but never called. Now a text box clicked (or focused from code with Control.Focus) takes the island's keyboard; the one losing it gets LostFocus and the new one GotFocus, both routed up the tree; FocusState follows. The island's key messages become KeyDown and KeyUp (KeyRoutedEventArgs: Key, KeyStatus, Handled, OriginalKey, OriginalSource) routed up from the focused element (the root when none is) until a handler sets Handled; keys nobody handled edit a focused text box: typed characters (replacing a selection), Left, Right, Home, End, Back, Delete, Enter when it accepts returns, Ctrl+A, Ctrl+C/X/V through the clipboard; MaxLength and IsReadOnly hold. A focused box draws its caret where its text lays out the character (DirectWrite hit testing). Elements can draw over their children (elem_ops.render_over). Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT); the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
